## Final Mental Models

| Concept | Mental Model |
|---------|--------------|
| Hash ring | A clock face — keys are times, servers are hour markers. Each key belongs to whatever hour marker it hits next going clockwise. |
| Modulo hashing failure | Changing the number of slices on a pizza — almost every topping ends up on a different slice. |
| Virtual nodes | One person sitting at 5 different desks in an office — they get mail delivered to each desk, spreading the work. |
| Hot spot vs. structural imbalance | Structural = desks are unevenly spaced. Hot spot = one desk gets 100 packages while others get 2. Different problems, different fixes. |
| Replication + consistent hashing | Belt and suspenders — hashing decides where data lives, replication ensures it survives failures without moving. |

